  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the emergency COVID-19 response through improving access to basic needs and protection services for the most vulnerable and marginalised older women and men with and without
disabilities during the winter months in 4 governorates of Jordan.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve PSEA and access to related information and services for older men and women and other community members in target communities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preserve the ability of older men and women most vulnerable to the pandemic to meet their food consumption and other basic needs during the winter months</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed 4-month emergency response project aims at improving access to basic needs and protection services for the most vulnerable and marginalised older women and men with and without disabilities during the winter months and to help them cope with the secondary impacts of COVID-19, in Amman, Mafraq, Zarqa, and Irbid.
The project will provide cash assistance to support 800 of the most vulnerable older people (70% of older women) and their family members in meeting their basic needs, in particular food, medication for chronic disease as well as heating costs for the winter months. Through cash assistance, the project will help mitigate the negative impact of the pandemic. Protection will be mainstreamed throughout the project implementation to ensure safe and meaningful access to cash for older people, while preserving their dignity. In addition, the project will put a special focus on PSEA and age and gender based violence; it will ensure that all staff and volunteers involved in the project and members of target
communities are well aware of PSEA and age and gender-based violence, as well as safeguarding concerns, and how reports can be made safely.</narrative>
  </description>
